  "problem": {
    "id": "train-3293",
    "question": "Carl is taking a class where the whole grade is based on four tests that are graded out of 100. He got an 80, a 75 and a 90 on his first three tests. If he wants an 85 average for the class, what is the minimum grade he needs to get on his last test?",
    "gold": "95",
    "answer": "First, find the total number of points Carl needs to earn across all the tests by multiplying his desired average by the number of tests: 85 * 4 = <<85*4=340>>340 marks.\nThen subtract all Carl's previous test scores to find the last score he needs to earn: 340 - 80 - 75 - 90 = <<340-80-75-90=95>>95 marks.\n#### 95"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the minimum grade Carl needs on his last test to achieve an average of 85, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total score Carl needs for an average of 85:**\n   The average of four tests is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of all test scores}}{\\text{Number of tests}}\n   \\]\n   Carl wants an average of 85, and he has four tests. Therefore, the total score he needs is:\n   \\[\n   85 \\times 4 = 340\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the sum of the scores Carl has already received:**\n   Carl has taken three tests with scores of 80, 75, and 90. The sum of these scores is:\n   \\[\n   80 + 75 + 90 = 245\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the score Carl needs on his last test:**\n   Let \\( x \\) be the score Carl needs on his last test. The sum of all four test scores will be:\n   \\[\n   245 + x\n   \\]\n   We know this sum must equal 340 for an average of 85. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   245 + x = 340\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   x = 340 - 245 = 95\n   \\]\n\nThus, the minimum grade Carl needs to get on his last test to achieve an average of 85 is \\(\\boxed{95}\\).",
